        <briefdescription>
<para>Convert a double to a string. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>                        Matches the output of the former ostk::core::type::Real::toString:
                        NaN is printed as &quot;Undefined&quot;, infinities as &quot;+Inf&quot; / &quot;-Inf&quot;.
                        With a negative precision, the shortest round-trip representation is used
                        (integral values get a &quot;.0&quot; suffix, trailing zeros are removed).
                        With a non-negative precision, fixed notation with that many decimals is used.
</verbatim></para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1mathematics_1_1utility_1a9497030ebeab9a401e6133d3ec9d1dd6" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(1.0)<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;1.0&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1mathematics_1_1utility_1a9497030ebeab9a401e6133d3ec9d1dd6" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(0.5)<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;0.5&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1mathematics_1_1utility_1a9497030ebeab9a401e6133d3ec9d1dd6" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(0.5,<sp/>3)<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;0.500&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1mathematics_1_1utility_1a9497030ebeab9a401e6133d3ec9d1dd6" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(std::numeric_limits&lt;double&gt;::quiet_NaN())<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;Undefined&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
